The Roundhat Gang is a protection racket in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]. It was run by [[Tywelwyn Leatherhide]] out of [[The Crowded Flea]] until his death. Whether the gang has survived him is not known. Recently, it appears to have established some kind of partnership with [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]].

Under [[Tywelwyn Leatherhide]], the Roundhat Gang operated with whatever authority its leader's reputation could command.

The gang are [[Bestiary/Werecreature|werecreatures]]. Each member has something of an animal about him on top of human stock, and they turn into boars, rats, crocodiles, tigers, bears and bats. They wear round hats, and the bouncer's round hat at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|The Crowded Flea]] marks the tavern as theirs. The half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] spoke for the gang to outsiders until he was killed in a [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] alley.

Its protection racket reaches businesses across Sableclutch, including the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Second Sun Diner|Second Sun Diner]], whose rooftop dish the gang installed. When the endless rain flooded the district, Tywelwyn moved his people out of it.

Tywelwyn is dead, a burnt husk by the end, killed with the gang members guarding him in the fane beneath a [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] auto body shop at 412 Anchor Boulevard in Widdershins. Past his throne the fane goes deeper, into a seven-sided room whose [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/An Iron Gauntlet in a Glass Glove|Heart]] had belonged to him. A shift crew of the gang came to the shop at ten each night in one car and went down to the fane; that crew is also dead.

The ledgers in Tywelwyn's office record the gang's fronts: the Gas-n-Go shop, two other Gas-n-Go franchises, the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]], two laundromats, a churro restaurant and a fried chicken restaurant.
